        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-attacks-on-beirut-much-bigger-than-anything-we-ve-seen-in-this-war-or-the-previous-one",
        "orario": "17:52",
        "timestamp": 1775663525,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel's attacks on Beirut 'much bigger than anything we've seen in this war or the previous one' Middle East Issued on: 08/04/2026 - 17:52 Nadia Massih is pleased to welcome Rania Abouzeid, Lebanese Australian independent journalist and veteran war reporter. Ms. Abouzeid describes \"chaotic scenes\" in the Lebanese capital. Israel's attacks on Beirut have been extensive and they are now targeting areas well beyond the southern suburbs: \"crowded, mixed sectarian residential areas that are full of the displaced\". Women and parentless children are flooding hospitals. Amid the \"simultaneous boom, boom, boom, strike after strike\" there are \"massive traffic jams… people just wanted to flee, but flee where?” 'Unlawful' war on Iran: 'Use of force by the United States never justified' 08/04/2026 Middle East US war on Iran: Lucas makes case for 'discussions & dialogue over renewing violence & confrontation' 08/04/2026 Middle East US-Iran ceasefire ‘a major problem domestically’ for Netanyahu 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran portraying ceasefire as 'victory against the United States and Israel' 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran positively reviewing Pakistan’s request for a two-week ceasefire, source says 07/04/2026 Middle East Trump's 'rhetoric itself could create a norm' for others to terrorise entire populations 07/04/2026 Middle East An 'eerie still' in Tehran amid Trump's apocalyptic threats 07/04/2026 Middle East Trump warns a 'whole civilization will die tonight' if a deal with Iran isn't reached 07/04/2026 Middle East Shootout outside Israeli consulate in Istanbul 07/04/2026 Middle East"
